WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.340
- In this present crisis,

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.980
government is not the
solution to our problem.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.633
Government is the problem.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.990
- Ask not what your
country can do for you.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.819
Ask what you can do for your country.

00:00:17.819 --> 00:00:21.024
(crowd applauding)

00:00:21.024 --> 00:00:23.340
- We've had this event during wars,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.040
we've had it during depressions.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.550
We'll have it during a pandemic.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.600
As President Reagan said the
first time he was sworn in

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.010
40 years ago that this event

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.157
is both commonplace and miraculous.

00:00:36.157 --> 00:00:39.100
Commonplace because we've
done it every four years

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.150
since 1789 and miraculous

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:46.120
because we've done it every
four years since 1789.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.000
- [Reporter] Against the
backdrop of a pandemic,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.090
January 20th, 2021 was set

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:54.900
to be an inauguration
for the history books.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.270
That was before a pro-Trump
mob rampaged the US Capitol

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:00.440
on January 6th and disrupted the vote

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.543
to certify Joe Biden's 2020
presidential election win.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.590
- You now have an
inaugural that's literally

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:09.390
going to take place on
the steps of the Capitol

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:12.730
that was ransacked a few
days earlier by a mob

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:16.440
trying to prevent the very
inaugural that's taking place.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.890
I think there is a tendency

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.100
to kind of overstate the
drama of most moments.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.759
There's the tendency to hype
them a little bit, if you will.

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:25.980
I think this one is kind of hard to hype.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.700
I think the drama is legitimate.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.790
- [Reporter] While President-elect
Joe Biden's inauguration

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.710
will certainly look different,

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:34.750
the US has sworn in presidents at times

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:38.171
of high national drama and
deep political division before.

00:01:38.171 --> 00:01:41.841
So how will Biden's
moment fit into history?

00:01:41.841 --> 00:01:45.800
(triumphant fanfare music)

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.930
- We all know as Americans
what that tableau

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:48.930
is supposed to look like.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.820
A crowded dais with the new president

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.770
and the outgoing president both there

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.570
with a lot of dignitaries
and the Supreme Court

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:57.210
and a big crowd down below.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.880
We're not gonna have all of those things.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.100
- [Reporter] The coronavirus pandemic

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.110
has fundamentally changed how we live,

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:06.190
and the tradition of the
inauguration is not being spared.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:09.310
As the US nears 400,000
deaths from the virus,

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.787
the inaugural has been
adjusted dramatically.

00:02:11.787 --> 00:02:14.620
Guests will be limited, the
luncheon has been canceled,

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:16.540
and the parade will be virtual.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:17.790
Senator Roy Blunt chairs

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.670
the Congressional Inauguration Committee.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:23.220
- Inauguration of the
President of the United States.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.850
(crowd cheering)

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:26.640
I think we're gonna have
somewhere in the neighborhood

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.920
of 2,500 to 3,000 people
at the inauguration

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.453
as opposed to 200,000.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.070
- [Reporter] Following the Capitol riot,

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.800
security is being beefed up.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.100
At least 20,000 National
Guardsmen were sent

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.450
to Washington, D.C. ahead
of the inauguration.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.920
That's more than twice the number sent

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.680
for President Obama's inauguration

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.160
when security concerns were also high.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.330
- Both President-elect
Biden and I and his team

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:55.330
are in agreement that events
of the attack on the Capitol

00:02:55.987 --> 00:03:00.020
make it even more important
that we're outside,

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.590
we're at the place where people

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:05.103
are used to seeing the
inauguration of the president.

00:03:06.143 --> 00:03:07.931
- [Reporter] One president
who won't be attending

00:03:07.931 --> 00:03:11.210
is President Trump who, with
a week remaining in his term

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:12.520
became the first president

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.110
to be impeached for a second time.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.480
- [Nancy] On the table.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.470
- [Reporter] After he was
accused of encouraging a mob

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:20.373
to storm the Capitol in an
effort to overturn the election.

00:03:20.373 --> 00:03:22.255
- There's gonna be an air of tension.

00:03:22.255 --> 00:03:24.596
The question of whether
Democrats and Republicans,

00:03:24.596 --> 00:03:26.760
having just been through this trauma

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.180
at the Capitol together,

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:30.070
will look as if they're unified or not

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.210
will be a question hanging over an event

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:34.810
in which people always
put on a face of unity.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.544
Will that be the case this time or not?

00:03:37.544 --> 00:03:39.880
- I, Franklin Delano Roosevelt--

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.300
- [Reporter] Like many
presidents before him,

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.690
Biden will enter office at a time

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.340
of heightened national drama.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.050
- I, Gerald R. Ford do solemnly swear.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.070
- [Reporter] But some of
the most dramatic times

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:50.670
have seen some of the most memorable

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:52.840
inaugural addresses in history.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.250
Jump back to 1865.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.710
- Lincoln's second inaugural that occurred

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:00.410
during the Civil War produced

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:03.160
probably the greatest
inaugural speech of all.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:06.907
He said to the country, "It
is time to bind our wounds.

00:04:06.907 --> 00:04:09.740
"We must heal," and it
was exactly the message

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.010
the country needed to hear at that time.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:14.726
It's also one that stood the test of time.

00:04:14.726 --> 00:04:15.627
- Do solemnly swear.

00:04:15.627 --> 00:04:18.400
- [Reporter] Nearly 70
years later, the US,

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.150
in the midst of the Great Depression,

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:23.020
elected Franklin D.
Roosevelt for the first time.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:23.853
At his inauguration,

00:04:23.853 --> 00:04:26.710
he addressed the nation,
now famously saying.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:30.477
- The only thing we have
to fear is fear itself.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.577
- In both cases, Lincoln and Roosevelt

00:04:34.577 --> 00:04:36.620
were trying to persuade Americans

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.670
that the drama of the
moment could be overcome.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.860
- That is similar in
some ways to, I think,

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.800
the atmosphere we have now
where people are saying,

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.840
can our democracy survive?

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.493
The inaugurals are designed
to lift up Washington,

00:04:48.493 --> 00:04:51.580
a moment in which everybody
can be optimistic.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.230
We'll see if Joe Biden can pull off that

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:57.390
in this strange environment.
(audience applauding)

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:59.560
- [Reporter] In 2000, the
highly-contested election

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.350
between George W. Bush and Al Gore

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:03.080
went all the way to the Supreme Court

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.950
and wasn't decided until December,

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:06.590
a month before the inauguration.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:08.480
- [Matt Lauer] Finally, a president-elect.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:11.350
George W. Bush will
become the 43rd president

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:12.599
of the United States.

00:05:12.599 --> 00:05:15.340
- It fell to George W. Bush to say,

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.670
this is a divided country politically.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:20.010
There's controversy over my election.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:21.157
He didn't say it, but he knew

00:05:21.157 --> 00:05:24.010
that some people thought he
wasn't even legitimately elected

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.860
'cause he hadn't won the popular vote.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.561
He used his inaugural to say,

00:05:27.561 --> 00:05:30.160
I recognize that there are deep wounds

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.530
left by this election.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.320
I will help us all move past them.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:39.310
- Our unity, our union is
the serious work of leaders

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.823
and citizens and every generation.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.750
And this is my solemn pledge.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.200
I will work to build a single nation

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.912
of justice and opportunity.

00:05:50.912 --> 00:05:52.400
(audience applauding)

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.420
- [Reporter] Trump faced a
similarly divided country

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.760
when he took office in 2017.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:58.960
Like Bush, he won the Electoral College

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.970
but lost the popular vote.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.430
In his speech, however, he
took a different approach

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.100
in addressing this divide.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:08.990
- And the crime and
the gangs and the drugs

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:11.300
that have stolen too many lives

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:16.300
and robbed our country of so
much unrealized potential.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:22.090
This American carnage stops
right here and stops right now.

00:06:25.373 --> 00:06:26.980
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:28.160
- Rather than really trying

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:30.990
to soothe the political passions,

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.180
some ways he ramped 'em up.

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:36.910
He said basically America
is a place that is hurting.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:40.997
It has been hurt by you people,
the political establishment.

00:06:40.997 --> 00:06:44.150
There's a dark America out
there that needs to be changed.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.120
I'm going to change it.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:50.120
- From this day forward it's
going to be only America first.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:55.630
- [Reporter] Now as Biden takes office,

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:57.810
he is facing a still divided country.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.560
A poll last month found
roughly 1/3 of those surveyed

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:03.430
did not think Biden won
the election legitimately.

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:04.470
And about the same share

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:06.510
believe there was widespread voter fraud.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.920
- Just so you understand,
this election was a fraud.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:11.790
- [Reporter] Trump has repeated
both of these false claims.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.580
- He's conceded that he's not going

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:14.900
to be the president any longer,

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.640
but he has not conceded
that he lost the election.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:19.870
That is going to convey,

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.500
in the eyes of millions of Americans,

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.320
a sense of illegitimacy
about a President Biden

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.330
and the Biden administration.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:29.000
- [Reporter] This
inauguration seems poised

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.810
to hold a unique place
in our country's history.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:34.670
- [Gerald] How President
Biden tries to speak to people

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:37.190
who think he is not the
legitimate next president

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:38.990
of this country is going to be

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:40.912
an important part of this inaugural.

00:07:40.912 --> 00:07:43.440
- I pledge to be a president

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.680
who seeks not to divide but unify.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.100
- [Gerald] I think people will look back

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.490
on the 2021 inauguration
of Joe Biden and say,

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.180
that was the one and only inauguration

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.680
this country has ever
had that went that way.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.770
I can't imagine this set of circumstances

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:03.243
ever being repeated.
(soft instrumental music)

